  "text": "Two modern trends are widening this gap even further. First is prompt caching. System prompts, tool schemas, and codebase files repeat across calls, so servers reuse their precomputed KV cache and discount cached inputs up to ninety percent. Output tokens are freshly generated every time and can never be cached.",
